WEBVTT

03:08.939 --> 03:10.357
We're close.

03:37.009 --> 03:38.761
Ah! Ah...

03:41.347 --> 03:42.431
Aargh!

03:48.228 --> 03:49.855
I'll find a rock.

03:51.899 --> 03:52.942
Ah...

04:07.414 --> 04:08.999
It can't end like this...

04:40.614 --> 04:41.865
It's okay.

04:42.616 --> 04:43.993
Come here.

04:48.956 --> 04:50.499
There's nothing.

04:55.838 --> 04:57.464
Nothing to be done.

05:16.358 --> 05:18.027
Just turn away.

05:18.360 --> 05:19.695
Be still.

05:26.326 --> 05:28.037
I said turn away!

05:46.263 --> 05:47.430
Aaaargh!

08:10.115 --> 08:16.413
♪ Oft in the stilly night ♪

08:16.747 --> 08:23.712
♪ Ere slumber's chain
has bound me ♪

08:25.297 --> 08:31.010
♪ Fond memory
brings the light ♪

08:31.011 --> 08:37.684
♪ Of other days around me ♪

08:40.312 --> 08:43.189
♪ The smiles, the tears ♪

08:43.190 --> 08:45.734
♪ Of boyhood's years ♪

08:46.568 --> 08:51.240
♪ The words of love
then spoken ♪

08:53.408 --> 08:56.078
♪ The eyes that shone ♪

08:56.411 --> 08:59.748
♪ Now dimm'd and gone ♪

09:00.707 --> 09:06.129
♪ The cheerful hearts
now broken ♪

09:51.466 --> 09:52.968
Why'd you shoot it?

09:53.510 --> 09:54.970
They're pests.

09:55.262 --> 09:58.223
They jump up on the cars
and make shit of the paintwork.

09:59.308 --> 10:01.059
Couldn't just shoo it away, huh?

10:01.768 --> 10:03.061
Goats are stubborn.

10:04.604 --> 10:06.106
Spray it with a hose?

10:08.525 --> 10:09.526
No.

10:17.492 --> 10:18.784
I'm telling you now, Fergal,

10:18.785 --> 10:20.453
I'm not dragging that
into the woods.

10:20.454 --> 10:21.330
Shut up.

10:21.663 --> 10:23.457
Fado, fado...

10:23.915 --> 10:27.001
Long, long ago,
deep in the woods,

10:27.002 --> 10:29.296
there was a small stone hut.

10:29.796 --> 10:32.131
And inside the stone hut,

10:32.132 --> 10:35.302
there lived an old Cailleach...

10:36.511 --> 10:37.888
A witch.

10:38.847 --> 10:40.766
Preying upon the lost,

10:40.932 --> 10:44.185
the evil old crone would first
put the doomed travellers

10:44.186 --> 10:45.729
under her spell,

10:46.021 --> 10:50.233
leaving them as dazzled
and vulnerable as lamplit game.

10:52.277 --> 10:55.488
The witch would then shackle
her stunned prey

10:55.489 --> 10:58.115
before taking
the lost travellers

10:58.116 --> 11:00.535
on a tour of the underworld.

11:01.453 --> 11:03.120
And sometimes,

11:03.121 --> 11:06.874
a hand or a claw
would reach out from the dark

11:06.875 --> 11:10.879
and tear a piece from those
at the end of her chain.

11:11.588 --> 11:13.173
Pluck out an eye.

11:13.882 --> 11:15.300
Peel off an ear.

11:16.843 --> 11:18.219
And sometimes,

11:18.220 --> 11:20.805
they took something
from a little boy

11:20.806 --> 11:24.559
that was more valuable to him
than his eyes or ears.

11:25.727 --> 11:30.022
Any guesses which part of you
that might be?

11:31.441 --> 11:33.443
- These your kids?
- No.

11:35.779 --> 11:37.155
Go find your parents.

11:39.116 --> 11:41.326
And don't talk
to strangers again.

11:44.246 --> 11:47.749
There are worse things
than strangers out there, Yank.

11:52.254 --> 11:53.880
Did we wake you?

11:54.005 --> 11:55.632
Uh, Mr Cob, my apologies.

11:55.966 --> 11:58.342
I was on the phone and I thought
Alby was manning...

11:58.343 --> 12:00.719
Don't apologise to me,
you maneen.

12:00.720 --> 12:02.431
Apologise to the guest!

12:02.889 --> 12:04.056
My apologies.

12:04.057 --> 12:05.641
Why don't you mind
your own business?

12:05.642 --> 12:06.726
It is my business.

12:07.853 --> 12:09.438
I'm the owner.

12:11.189 --> 12:13.357
Bauman. I have a reservation.

12:13.358 --> 12:17.611
If you could just sign...
Ah! Mr Bauman.

12:17.612 --> 12:20.031
Mr Ohm Bauman,
Pullman City, Washington.

12:20.157 --> 12:22.700
With us for a week. Welcome.

12:22.701 --> 12:24.369
Lock it up.

12:26.621 --> 12:28.415
Alby's dragging it out
into the woods.

12:30.083 --> 12:32.961
Dining room is down
this corridor here.

12:33.420 --> 12:35.797
Breakfast in the morning
from seven to ten.

12:35.964 --> 12:38.466
Halloween party tomorrow night
with live music,

12:38.467 --> 12:40.259
cocktails, costumes...

12:40.260 --> 12:41.636
Should be a bit of craic.

12:41.845 --> 12:44.513
Oh, um, craic is a word we use

12:44.514 --> 12:46.307
to describe a fun time
here in Ireland.

12:46.308 --> 12:47.850
Yeah, can I get a room
as far away

12:47.851 --> 12:49.978
from the 'craic' as possible?

12:50.312 --> 12:52.647
- I've work to do.
- What do you do?

12:52.856 --> 12:54.024
Writer.

12:55.859 --> 12:57.152
Well...

12:58.278 --> 12:59.737
you shouldn't hear a thing.

12:59.738 --> 13:00.739
Thank you.

13:02.491 --> 13:05.035
Wait... Bauman.

13:05.202 --> 13:07.162
Ah, I know that name.

13:07.996 --> 13:10.790
I think my son
is a fan of yours!

13:11.791 --> 13:13.293
A celebrity.

13:14.085 --> 13:15.377
Well, if there's anything
we can do

13:15.378 --> 13:17.213
to make your stay
more enjoyable,

13:17.214 --> 13:19.633
please dial '0' and let us know.

13:19.758 --> 13:20.967
All right.

13:21.384 --> 13:23.552
Oh, maybe I could bring in
my son's book

13:23.553 --> 13:24.846
and you could sign it for him?

13:25.847 --> 13:26.932
No.

13:37.776 --> 13:39.569
There's nothing
getting through that.

13:39.986 --> 13:41.530
That's built to last.

13:53.083 --> 13:55.168
Oh, for fuck's sake.

13:55.377 --> 13:56.920
Are you lost?

13:57.254 --> 13:58.838
What does it look like?

13:59.047 --> 14:02.383
Well, with that attitude,
it looks like you can stay lost.

14:02.384 --> 14:04.718
Okay, sorry, I'm just...
I can't find my room.

14:04.719 --> 14:07.973
It should be right here,
but it's not.

14:08.807 --> 14:11.142
- Oh, yeah. It's this way.
- Thank you.

14:12.310 --> 14:14.729
- First time in Ireland?
- Yeah.

14:15.105 --> 14:16.815
Are you having a nice time?

14:17.315 --> 14:18.358
Yeah.

14:19.484 --> 14:21.069
This is you.

14:21.486 --> 14:22.612
Thank you.

14:22.862 --> 14:24.197
Enjoy your stay.

14:24.739 --> 14:27.158
Thanks. Oh, hey...

14:27.867 --> 14:30.662
Sorry, would you happen to know

14:31.871 --> 14:34.958
with the Big Redwood is?

16:09.260 --> 16:10.929
- Who are those?
- Jesus...

16:13.973 --> 16:15.392
Oh, uh...

16:16.184 --> 16:17.602
My folks.

16:19.229 --> 16:20.647
Sorry for your loss.

16:22.774 --> 16:24.316
You want a drink?

16:24.317 --> 16:27.070
I think I may need something
stronger than milk.

16:31.574 --> 16:33.118
Nothing stronger than that.

16:35.412 --> 16:37.622
- Moonshine?
- Poitín.

16:38.081 --> 16:39.541
Uisce beatha.

16:39.874 --> 16:41.251
Water of life.

16:43.753 --> 16:46.047
Whoo. Yeah, that's moonshine.

16:46.965 --> 16:48.799
If you want something
to defeat the demons,

16:48.800 --> 16:50.510
and not just be
running from them.

16:51.052 --> 16:52.512
Magic mushrooms.

16:54.222 --> 16:55.682
Psilocybin.

16:56.266 --> 16:57.642
It's all natural.

16:58.643 --> 17:01.604
I pick, dry, and grind
the mushrooms myself.

17:02.689 --> 17:04.482
And I like it with goat's milk.

17:06.109 --> 17:07.776
What are you gonna do with it?

17:07.777 --> 17:09.862
- I'll bury her.
- Hm.

17:09.863 --> 17:12.240
Do you know why they climb
on the cars?

17:14.659 --> 17:17.494
Goats like to graze
on the mushrooms as well.

17:17.495 --> 17:18.912
And when they're coming up,

17:18.913 --> 17:23.001
they go looking for reflective
surfaces, 'cause...

17:24.085 --> 17:27.464
staring into your own eyes
on mushrooms

17:27.964 --> 17:29.716
deepens the trip.

17:30.925 --> 17:32.135
But...

17:32.886 --> 17:34.471
it can be dangerous.

17:34.763 --> 17:37.557
Especially if there's an asshole
with a crossbow nearby.

17:38.141 --> 17:39.641
Don't get me started.

17:39.642 --> 17:42.103
I've nearly come to blows
with him over it.

17:42.562 --> 17:43.772
Thanks for the drink.

17:45.940 --> 17:47.900
Don't go climbing up
on any cars.

17:47.901 --> 17:50.069
I won't!

18:06.795 --> 18:11.548
The boy's skull is the only hard
object for, like, miles.

18:11.549 --> 18:14.260
So, the conquistador

18:14.719 --> 18:17.889
hits the boy with the bottle,
killing him,

18:18.097 --> 18:21.100
but the bottle
still doesn't break.

18:22.310 --> 18:26.606
In the end, he wanders out
into the desert to die.

18:34.155 --> 18:36.491
- Why would you write this?
- What do you mean?

18:36.699 --> 18:39.160
I mean, it's so bleak.

18:39.285 --> 18:41.913
Well, you know, it's meant
to be challenging.

18:42.622 --> 18:46.501
Well, I won't be reading it.
Not if that's how it ends.

18:47.627 --> 18:49.253
Well, you know,
a few of my novels

18:49.254 --> 18:50.712
have been turned
into bad movies,

18:50.713 --> 18:53.173
and when they make
the movie for you,

18:53.174 --> 18:55.134
you tag on a happy ending.

18:55.468 --> 18:57.679
Okay, well, they'd better.

18:59.639 --> 19:01.766
You remind me of my mom.

19:02.892 --> 19:05.853
Your mum? How old
do you think I am?

19:05.854 --> 19:08.064
Well, when she was young,
you know.

19:10.775 --> 19:12.652
Yeah, just in the way she...

19:15.822 --> 19:17.824
Hm. She looks happy.

19:17.949 --> 19:19.909
My dad took that.

19:20.243 --> 19:21.952
You know, they came here
for their honeymoon.

19:21.953 --> 19:23.496
Always wanted to come back.

19:23.621 --> 19:25.038
- Oh yeah?
- Yeah.

19:25.039 --> 19:26.498
Why didn't they?

19:26.499 --> 19:28.918
Oh, she died a few years
after that.

19:30.086 --> 19:32.171
- She was very young.
- Mm.

19:32.338 --> 19:34.382
- How did she die?
- Murdered.

19:35.300 --> 19:38.428
Shot in the face
as she came home from work.

19:39.971 --> 19:41.889
Did they catch the person
that shot her?

19:41.890 --> 19:43.975
Nah, he's too young
to be punished.

19:44.225 --> 19:45.977
Should have fucking hanged him.

19:48.062 --> 19:49.564
And your dad?

19:50.106 --> 19:53.567
Oh, well, he...
turned into a monster

19:53.568 --> 19:55.486
and drank himself
to an early grave.

19:58.281 --> 20:01.366
You know, I've had
their ashes for years

20:01.367 --> 20:03.035
and never knew
what to do with them.

20:03.036 --> 20:05.204
I knew they were happy
here, so...

20:06.122 --> 20:09.751
Hey, I noticed the honeymoon
suite, it's closed.

20:10.501 --> 20:12.420
I wonder if that's the room
they stayed in.

20:12.754 --> 20:15.298
That has been closed
a long time.

20:15.757 --> 20:17.175
Do you know why?

20:17.383 --> 20:21.012
Because no couple in their right
mind would honeymoon here?

20:21.429 --> 20:22.931
It's haunted.

20:24.140 --> 20:26.517
- Oh.
- By a witch.

20:27.352 --> 20:30.647
Mr Cob says they managed to lock
her in there years ago.

20:31.314 --> 20:35.233
I tried to convince Mal
to sneak the key off Mr Cob

20:35.234 --> 20:36.819
so I could have a look up there,

20:37.195 --> 20:39.822
but... he wouldn't go for it.

20:40.239 --> 20:44.159
I have never known a man to be
so afraid of his father-in-law.

20:44.160 --> 20:45.869
Why do you want to go up there
so bad?

20:45.870 --> 20:47.829
To see if there really is
a witch up there.

20:47.830 --> 20:48.914
What if there is?

20:48.915 --> 20:50.374
I mean, aren't you
afraid she'll,

20:50.375 --> 20:51.709
uh, 'get you'?

20:57.215 --> 21:00.133
- I'd bring some chalk.
- Chalk?

21:00.134 --> 21:02.719
If you ever find yourself
being chased by a witch,

21:02.720 --> 21:04.846
draw a circle around you.
Keep you safe.

21:04.847 --> 21:06.807
If I ever think I'm being chased
by a witch,

21:06.808 --> 21:10.060
I will look for a psychiatrist,
not a piece of chalk.

21:11.646 --> 21:13.438
Oh, perfect. Alby...

21:13.439 --> 21:15.273
Tell Ohm here about
your encounter

21:15.274 --> 21:16.693
with the witch upstairs.

21:19.112 --> 21:20.488
Well, um...

21:38.381 --> 21:39.632
Hello?

22:36.773 --> 22:38.107
And that's what happened.

22:39.358 --> 22:40.693
Hokum.

22:42.028 --> 22:43.571
Don't worry, Alby.

22:43.780 --> 22:44.906
I believe you.

22:46.324 --> 22:48.493
Fiona?
Delivery to sign for.

22:51.162 --> 22:52.455
Back in a sec.

22:55.833 --> 22:57.919
Are you enjoying your stay,
Mr Bauman?

22:59.128 --> 23:00.421
Yeah, I guess.

23:01.923 --> 23:05.093
When I saw the name, I didn't
think it would actually be you.

23:05.635 --> 23:07.261
Uh, what are you doing here?

23:08.596 --> 23:10.056
Who knows?

23:11.140 --> 23:13.517
I don't mean to bother you,
but I wanted to tell you

23:13.518 --> 23:15.103
how much your books
have meant to me.

23:15.436 --> 23:17.437
I really relate
to your characters.

23:17.438 --> 23:18.688
Well, that's troubling,

23:18.689 --> 23:20.857
seeing as those pages
are populated

23:20.858 --> 23:24.529
by deeply disturbed,
desperate people.

23:25.613 --> 23:28.491
Oh, is that what you use to keep
track of all your ideas?

23:29.742 --> 23:31.118
It is, yeah.

23:31.119 --> 23:34.914
And in fact, I just had one
speaking with you.

23:38.042 --> 23:39.960
Idea for a character,

23:39.961 --> 23:43.422
uh, oblivious charisma vacuum.

23:44.340 --> 23:48.719
Is completely incapable
of reading a room.

23:49.679 --> 23:50.930
Ah...

23:51.931 --> 23:54.558
Is it true, I read
that you're finally writing

23:54.559 --> 23:56.184
the end of the Conquistador
trilogy?

23:56.185 --> 23:57.770
How fuck do I know
what you read?

23:58.020 --> 24:00.565
No, I mean, is it true you're
finally writing the ending?

24:01.482 --> 24:04.068
I'm starting to think
it's gonna be open-ended.

24:04.443 --> 24:06.529
And are you happy
with how it's going?

24:08.489 --> 24:09.907
I'm a writer too.

24:10.366 --> 24:13.035
And some nights it's hard
to face that blank page.

24:16.038 --> 24:17.165
Yeah.

24:18.291 --> 24:20.877
So that's a Halloween costume
you're wearing?

24:22.086 --> 24:23.837
Oh, uh, no.

24:23.838 --> 24:25.630
I-I just work here
to pay the bills.

24:25.631 --> 24:29.468
Oh. Oh, okay. So you're not
a writer, you're a bellboy.

24:30.720 --> 24:34.139
No, I am a writer. I just
don't get paid for it yet.

24:34.140 --> 24:35.682
- Ah.
- You know, it can be hard

24:35.683 --> 24:38.518
to get publishers or agents
or anybody to read anything.

24:38.519 --> 24:39.770
Sure.

24:41.272 --> 24:43.857
And actually, um, I've got
a manuscript in my locker.

24:43.858 --> 24:45.483
Do you mind if I ask you
to take a look at it?

24:45.484 --> 24:46.485
Nope.

24:46.819 --> 24:48.695
Why not?

24:48.696 --> 24:50.614
Ah! Jesus...

24:50.615 --> 24:51.990
You need thicker skin than that

24:51.991 --> 24:53.784
if you wanna make it
as a writer.

24:58.748 --> 25:00.124
What happened to you?

25:07.381 --> 25:08.883
What happened there?

25:09.383 --> 25:10.927
Never meet your heroes.

25:12.136 --> 25:13.387
I'll take another.

25:13.721 --> 25:15.348
And that'll be his last one.

25:21.479 --> 25:23.189
To bleak endings.

25:49.715 --> 25:50.716
Alby?

25:53.844 --> 25:55.096
Can you open this?

25:56.764 --> 25:59.474
I know, I'm just getting
a weird feeling.

25:59.475 --> 26:01.810
He's not answering.
- By the way he was drinking,

26:01.811 --> 26:04.105
he's probably passed out
in a pool of his own piss.

26:04.397 --> 26:05.814
He burnt my hand...

26:05.815 --> 26:06.899
Would you just open it!

26:10.403 --> 26:11.779
Your funeral.

26:16.033 --> 26:17.493
Mr Bauman?

26:19.912 --> 26:21.163
It's Fiona.

26:22.331 --> 26:24.125
You left your things in the bar.

26:25.543 --> 26:27.211
Mr Bauman?

26:29.338 --> 26:31.048
Jesus Christ! Alby!

28:32.086 --> 28:34.588
Thanks very much for your time,
Guards.

28:40.261 --> 28:41.345
Mr Bauman...

28:41.971 --> 28:43.347
Are you closing?

28:43.806 --> 28:45.182
End of season.

28:45.891 --> 28:47.685
How, uh...

28:48.811 --> 28:51.272
- How are you feeling?
- I'm sorry.

28:53.023 --> 28:55.818
I just, uh,
came to get my stuff.

28:56.485 --> 28:57.403
Of course.

28:57.778 --> 29:00.406
It's just, uh, back here,
safe and sound.

29:05.494 --> 29:06.829
Thank you.

29:12.376 --> 29:13.794
Hey, uh...

29:14.753 --> 29:16.046
Who found me?

29:17.673 --> 29:21.385
One of, uh,
the members of staff, Fiona.

29:21.719 --> 29:23.470
She was working in the bar
that night.

29:23.471 --> 29:26.098
Christ... Is she around?

29:27.308 --> 29:28.600
No.

29:28.601 --> 29:32.353
Well, I'd like to talk
to her. Apologise.

29:32.354 --> 29:34.106
Could I get her number?

29:34.732 --> 29:38.861
Uh, Mr Bauman, um,
Fiona's missing.

29:39.153 --> 29:40.571
What do you mean?

29:41.739 --> 29:43.907
She hasn't been seen
since Halloween,

29:43.908 --> 29:45.743
and that's weeks ago.

29:46.076 --> 29:47.243
What?

29:50.414 --> 29:53.124
We thought maybe
she just wanted some time

29:53.125 --> 29:55.044
and didn't let
anybody know, but...

29:56.420 --> 29:58.255
What do they think
happened to her?

29:58.422 --> 29:59.715
They don't know.

30:00.257 --> 30:01.591
Well...

30:01.592 --> 30:04.052
Okay, but she couldn't
have just disappeared.

30:04.053 --> 30:07.096
I mean, they searched the hotel?
- Of course.

30:07.097 --> 30:08.432
And the woods.

30:08.766 --> 30:10.309
Could she have been taken?

30:10.643 --> 30:11.685
By who?

30:12.269 --> 30:13.770
Well, how the fuck
should I know?

30:13.771 --> 30:18.775
I mean... local weirdo,
a guest, someone who works here?

30:18.776 --> 30:20.777
I mean, I don't know
if you've noticed

30:20.778 --> 30:23.655
but there are some oddballs
walking around this place.

30:23.656 --> 30:24.823
Okay.

30:26.283 --> 30:29.703
Those men...
they were police.

30:30.120 --> 30:32.038
And there is a man
that they wanna speak with

30:32.039 --> 30:34.041
who lives in the woods.
His name is Jerry.

30:35.167 --> 30:38.671
Fergal saw Fiona outside talking
to him earlier that night.

30:39.380 --> 30:40.756
He hasn't been seen since.

30:42.258 --> 30:46.387
Now, we always just considered
him a pest around here.

30:46.554 --> 30:49.264
He comes into the hotel,
sits by the fire,

30:49.265 --> 30:51.016
bothers the guests.
- Right.

30:52.309 --> 30:54.602
Since his disappearance,

30:54.603 --> 30:57.189
the Guards have learned
who Jerry is, and...

30:58.315 --> 31:02.110
it turns out Jerry disappeared
after his wife died

31:02.111 --> 31:04.363
under suspicious circumstances
ten years ago.

31:07.700 --> 31:10.619
Mr Bauman, I think
you've been through enough.

31:11.328 --> 31:13.413
Go home. Heal.

31:13.414 --> 31:16.166
I promise I'll call you myself
if there's any updates.

31:20.462 --> 31:22.630
I bet you have a whole
new appreciation

31:22.631 --> 31:24.508
for a woman's intuition.

31:26.343 --> 31:28.886
Alby told me that Fiona made him
unlock your door

31:28.887 --> 31:30.848
because she had a bad feeling.

31:31.432 --> 31:32.891
Lucky boy.

31:33.225 --> 31:35.643
You saw Fiona talking
to the man in the woods

31:35.644 --> 31:37.271
before she disappeared?

31:37.438 --> 31:40.649
Jerry. I warned her before
to stay away from him.

31:41.442 --> 31:45.446
Yeah, Mal said his wife died
under suspicious circumstances?

31:46.655 --> 31:48.073
Well, he obviously killed her,
didn't he?

31:49.533 --> 31:52.368
Why else would he be down here
hiding in the woods for years,

31:52.369 --> 31:53.996
living out of an old van.

31:54.663 --> 31:56.497
Oh, well, now he's gone.

31:56.498 --> 31:57.875
He'll be back.

31:59.376 --> 32:00.919
And I'll be waiting for him.

32:02.588 --> 32:04.715
Did you talk to her that night?

32:05.674 --> 32:07.175
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

32:07.176 --> 32:09.178
Wh... How'd she seem?

32:09.553 --> 32:11.138
Well, not herself.

32:12.348 --> 32:13.807
Distracted.

32:14.266 --> 32:15.434
Sad.

32:15.934 --> 32:18.979
I think she was still in shock
from having to cut you down.

32:24.401 --> 32:26.111
Okay, what about
the honeymoon suite?

32:26.904 --> 32:28.030
What about it?

32:28.155 --> 32:30.490
Well, was it searched?

32:30.491 --> 32:32.825
I mean, Fiona mentioned
wanting to go up there.

32:32.826 --> 32:35.036
Impossible.
The gate is always locked.

32:35.037 --> 32:37.247
Mr Cob has the key on him
at all times.

32:38.666 --> 32:40.125
So it wasn't searched?

32:41.210 --> 32:43.379
It's always locked.

32:45.130 --> 32:46.632
It's locked now.

32:47.132 --> 32:49.468
Mr Cob has me
check the gate every day.

32:50.761 --> 32:52.679
There's no way she could have
possibly got up there,

32:52.680 --> 32:55.516
so you might as well suggest
that we search the moon.

32:57.351 --> 32:58.977
Police talk to you?

33:03.023 --> 33:04.983
I talk to the Guards every day.

33:05.859 --> 33:07.444
My first cousins.

33:08.028 --> 33:10.155
Guarda Sergeant is my uncle.

33:11.365 --> 33:12.491
Why do you ask?

33:20.666 --> 33:22.793
See, the best thing
you could do now,

33:24.086 --> 33:25.796
is get into your car

33:25.921 --> 33:27.839
and fuck off back to the airport

33:27.840 --> 33:30.134
while you still look like
your passport picture.

33:37.725 --> 33:39.059
Safe home now.

34:02.082 --> 34:03.333
Come on!

35:01.809 --> 35:04.603
Jesus fucking Christ!

35:04.937 --> 35:07.064
Fiona'd be glad to know
you woke up.

35:07.648 --> 35:09.483
Okay, well, she's missing.

35:12.569 --> 35:14.028
Do you have anything
to do with that?

35:14.029 --> 35:15.113
No.

35:16.865 --> 35:18.366
Well, the police
are looking for you.

35:18.367 --> 35:20.577
You're the last one
seen talking to her.

35:21.286 --> 35:22.662
I don't think it's
the only reason

35:22.663 --> 35:24.206
they're looking for me now.

35:24.957 --> 35:26.041
Huh?

35:26.375 --> 35:28.710
Yeah, that's right.
They said you killed your wife.

35:29.294 --> 35:31.630
Yeah, that's true.

35:33.257 --> 35:35.217
She was very ill.

35:35.884 --> 35:38.262
She was in a lot of pain.

35:40.764 --> 35:42.140
You know...

35:43.350 --> 35:46.060
this is Fiona's.
- We were friends.

35:46.061 --> 35:47.771
She let me borrow it.

35:49.022 --> 35:50.440
Oh, she did?

35:51.066 --> 35:53.860
Okay, well, why don't you
come with me

35:53.861 --> 35:55.945
and we'll talk to the police.

35:55.946 --> 35:57.823
No, it's pointless.

35:57.948 --> 35:59.950
They-they wouldn't
believe me anyway.

36:00.158 --> 36:01.326
Oh yeah?

36:01.451 --> 36:03.078
Why? What do you think
happened to her?

36:03.412 --> 36:04.830
I don't know.

36:05.205 --> 36:06.874
But I know she's dead.

36:09.418 --> 36:11.085
Why do you say that?

36:11.086 --> 36:12.503
There's a cupboard
in Mal's office

36:12.504 --> 36:14.131
full of medicine
left behind by guests.

36:15.215 --> 36:18.135
Two nights ago,
I went there to stock up...

36:19.344 --> 36:21.263
I-I saw her.

37:18.737 --> 37:20.112
What?

37:20.113 --> 37:22.198
And-and the bell
she was pointing to,

37:22.199 --> 37:24.408
it's an old mechanical call bell

37:24.409 --> 37:26.578
connected to the honeymoon
suite.

37:28.580 --> 37:31.541
I think she was trying
to tell me to go up there.

37:34.503 --> 37:36.128
I'm waiting till
the hotel's empty

37:36.129 --> 37:37.422
and then I'm going up there
to check.

37:37.923 --> 37:41.009
Okay, but unless you have a key,
then how the hell...

37:41.927 --> 37:43.719
Ah, right. Of course.

37:43.720 --> 37:46.389
Cob lives on the other side
of the woods. I broke in.

37:46.390 --> 37:48.975
But if he had the key,
then she couldn't be up there.

37:48.976 --> 37:50.893
No, unless someone stole it,

37:50.894 --> 37:53.522
took her up there and then put
it back without him noticing.

37:53.855 --> 37:55.356
Right, but who would do that?

37:55.357 --> 37:56.316
I don't know!

37:58.276 --> 38:00.778
Okay. Why don't you
give it to me?

38:00.779 --> 38:02.697
I'll go back and I'll check.
- No, you-you...

38:02.698 --> 38:04.532
You wouldn't even
get near the gate

38:04.533 --> 38:06.033
with Fergal or Mal still there.

38:06.034 --> 38:07.703
No. It has to be at night.

38:08.078 --> 38:09.287
Tonight...

38:10.080 --> 38:11.915
when the hotel is empty.

38:15.919 --> 38:17.462
Would you come with me?

38:19.506 --> 38:22.300
I don't know what I'm gonna find
when I get up there.

38:23.010 --> 38:25.887
I'd rather not go alone.

38:30.684 --> 38:33.437
You know all these things
do exist?

38:36.815 --> 38:40.318
It is just people
with closed minds can't see 'em.

38:45.866 --> 38:49.369
There's one more car
to pass by my count,

38:49.745 --> 38:51.747
then the hotel is empty.

38:52.539 --> 38:55.375
You really think that was
Fiona's ghost that you saw?

38:56.084 --> 38:57.335
Yeah.

38:57.753 --> 39:01.339
Were you drinking your magic
milk when you saw this ghost?

39:02.382 --> 39:04.176
That's how I saw her.

39:04.551 --> 39:06.511
My mind was open.

39:08.889 --> 39:10.599
What the fuck am I doing here?

39:12.476 --> 39:15.645
My wife's spirit
visited me once on a trip.

39:18.690 --> 39:21.359
She thanked me
for ending her suffering.

39:22.652 --> 39:25.197
Said we'd be together
again someday.

39:30.077 --> 39:31.411
Whatever you say, man.

39:34.206 --> 39:36.917
She said we'd be together again.

39:38.960 --> 39:40.504
Believe what you want.

39:46.426 --> 39:48.385
When we go up there, yeah,

39:48.386 --> 39:50.597
and we find Fiona...

39:51.139 --> 39:52.808
you'll believe it too.

39:53.642 --> 39:55.227
And what if we don't find her?

39:56.394 --> 39:58.605
Does that mean all of this
is just in your head?

40:06.988 --> 40:08.115
Okay.

40:48.864 --> 40:51.283
Hey, she-she was kind
of like this.

40:52.742 --> 40:55.161
- Come on.
- Just getting the crossbow.

40:55.162 --> 40:57.037
What? Don't go get that!
We don't need that!

40:58.165 --> 40:59.416
Shit.

41:17.142 --> 41:18.518
Ugh...

41:40.498 --> 41:42.125
Is there someone there?

42:00.644 --> 42:03.730
- Garda Station?
- Áine? It's Fergal.

42:04.231 --> 42:05.357
I have Jerry.

42:05.482 --> 42:07.066
Tell my cousins
I'm bringing him in.

42:07.067 --> 42:08.525
What do you mean,
'you have him'?

42:08.526 --> 42:10.779
- I have to get on the road.
- What? Fergal, no...

45:24.055 --> 45:25.640
Jesus...

47:28.471 --> 47:29.681
Uh...

47:43.319 --> 47:45.613
It's all right, it's all right.

47:46.072 --> 47:47.574
What are you doing here?

47:47.740 --> 47:49.158
You're asking me?

47:50.410 --> 47:52.786
I got a phone call from Mr Cob
in a panic

47:52.787 --> 47:54.872
saying the honeymoon key
was missing.

48:00.920 --> 48:02.588
How'd you even get this?

48:02.589 --> 48:04.424
- Jerry?
- Jerry.

48:04.674 --> 48:06.926
Yeah, he's convinced
Fiona was up here.

48:08.219 --> 48:10.013
Where is he?

48:10.471 --> 48:12.681
Fergal, the fuckhead,
took him to the police.

48:12.682 --> 48:14.017
He didn't see me.

48:15.435 --> 48:16.811
What were you thinking?

48:18.062 --> 48:20.439
Uh, she saved me.
I wanted to help find her.

48:20.440 --> 48:21.441
I don't know.

48:23.610 --> 48:24.944
Okay.

48:25.111 --> 48:27.739
Why don't we just go downstairs?

48:27.864 --> 48:29.531
We'll get in trouble
if we're caught up here.

48:29.532 --> 48:30.617
Alright.

48:31.909 --> 48:33.994
Can you gimme a ride
back to my car?

48:33.995 --> 48:34.996
Yeah.

48:42.128 --> 48:44.172
You're lucky
you didn't get locked in here.

48:44.297 --> 48:46.715
Mr Cob told me a story
about a young bride

48:46.716 --> 48:48.176
locking herself in here once.

48:50.928 --> 48:52.554
Oh no, Mr Bauman...

48:52.555 --> 48:54.390
Mr Bauman, would you please?

48:54.557 --> 48:56.559
You're not supposed
to be up here!

48:56.809 --> 49:00.063
Mr Cob is very strict
on people not coming up here!

49:00.271 --> 49:01.813
I could lose my job!

49:01.814 --> 49:03.232
Where does this go?

49:04.150 --> 49:07.069
There was a basement down there
before it was a hotel.

49:07.070 --> 49:07.986
Uh-huh.

49:07.987 --> 49:08.862
The entrance was lost

49:08.863 --> 49:09.863
during the renovations.

49:09.864 --> 49:11.115
There's nothing down there.

49:13.701 --> 49:14.827
Oh, look at that.

49:16.371 --> 49:18.706
There is nothing down there.

49:27.256 --> 49:30.635
No! Okay, okay.
We need to move, move.

49:30.927 --> 49:32.387
We need to leave!

49:34.722 --> 49:38.392
Mr Bauman, I am going to have
you arrested for trespassing

49:38.393 --> 49:39.893
if you do not leave
right this minute!

49:55.201 --> 49:56.160
Oh...

50:13.803 --> 50:15.805
Hey!

50:29.902 --> 50:31.487
Hey!

50:32.989 --> 50:34.157
Hey!

51:14.363 --> 51:16.240
Idea for a character.

51:17.325 --> 51:20.787
Uh, oblivious charisma vacuum.

51:22.580 --> 51:25.792
Completely incapable
of reading a room.

51:33.424 --> 51:34.634
Hi, girls.

51:35.301 --> 51:36.677
Looking well.

51:40.431 --> 51:42.141
I thought you were gonna
hand that in to the hospital.

51:46.854 --> 51:49.023
He's, uh, famous, you know?

51:49.357 --> 51:51.776
I bet you he'll dedicate his new
book to you if he wakes up.

51:51.901 --> 51:53.736
Don't say 'if', Mal.

51:58.658 --> 52:00.535
Drink your tea
while it's still hot.

52:19.512 --> 52:21.347
- Uh...
- You all right?

52:23.140 --> 52:24.475
I feel...

52:25.768 --> 52:27.061
I feel off.

53:03.180 --> 53:04.974
I'm grateful for it, you know,
it looks awesome.

53:08.811 --> 53:10.478
I can't see a thing
in it, man.

53:10.479 --> 53:11.981
It's absolutely sweating...

53:24.619 --> 53:26.537
It's alright.

53:31.459 --> 53:32.543
Ah...

54:20.591 --> 54:22.426
I know I'm gonna be okay.

54:23.970 --> 54:26.472
I'm gonna leave this message
here just in case.

54:29.934 --> 54:31.811
My name is Fiona Crotty.

54:33.771 --> 54:36.774
I think I'm in the basement
of the hotel, but...

54:37.108 --> 54:38.359
I don't know.

54:44.782 --> 54:46.283
I'm pregnant.

54:49.662 --> 54:52.873
Mal, the manager,
is the father.

54:54.625 --> 54:56.961
He wasn't happy with me
for keeping the baby.

55:02.967 --> 55:05.136
I wasn't gonna tell anyone
it was his,

55:08.347 --> 55:10.390
but he was just so terrified

55:10.391 --> 55:13.769
his wife or father-in-law,
Mr Cob, would find out.

55:15.688 --> 55:18.190
I can't believe
he'd go this far.

55:18.858 --> 55:20.484
Put us down here.

55:21.110 --> 55:22.528
Get rid of us.

55:28.367 --> 55:30.076
It's dark,

55:30.077 --> 55:32.997
but I'm gonna see
if I can find a way out.

55:33.664 --> 55:37.293
If I don't and someone
finds this message,

55:38.753 --> 55:40.421
tell my parents I love them.

57:07.508 --> 57:09.051
Fuckin' Fergal...

57:41.834 --> 57:42.918
Shit...

58:14.325 --> 58:15.868
No, no, no, no, no, no.

58:19.997 --> 58:21.081
Fuck!

58:21.373 --> 58:22.666
Fuck!

59:26.397 --> 59:27.690
Hello?

01:00:30.961 --> 01:00:31.920
Hey!

01:00:32.171 --> 01:00:33.297
Who's there?

01:01:11.418 --> 01:01:13.294
Aargh!

01:01:14.713 --> 01:01:19.801
Okay, kids, we're gonna read
our next letter!

01:01:19.802 --> 01:01:21.720
Yay!

01:01:22.054 --> 01:01:24.473
"Dear Jack..."
That's me!

01:01:24.848 --> 01:01:27.558
"My name is Ohm Bauman."

01:01:27.559 --> 01:01:28.894
Ohm? Okay.

01:01:29.645 --> 01:01:33.774
"I am ten years old
and my mom died last year."

01:01:34.525 --> 01:01:37.777
- What dies, kids?
- Everything!

01:01:37.778 --> 01:01:41.824
"I was playing with my dad's
gun and it went off."

01:01:42.408 --> 01:01:46.577
What are the two things
we don't ever play with, kids?

01:01:46.578 --> 01:01:48.246
- Fire!
- And?

01:01:48.247 --> 01:01:50.541
- Guns!
- That's right!

01:01:51.208 --> 01:01:53.460
"My dad hates me now."

01:01:53.669 --> 01:01:55.336
"I miss my mom."

01:01:55.337 --> 01:01:57.548
"I'm scared all the time."

01:01:57.673 --> 01:02:00.008
"Can you help me? Ohm."

01:02:00.843 --> 01:02:03.803
Well, Ohm, it's pretty simple.

01:02:03.804 --> 01:02:06.764
Your dad told you
not to go near his gun,

01:02:06.765 --> 01:02:08.891
but you did anyway.

01:02:08.892 --> 01:02:12.728
And his wife got her brains
blown out.

01:02:14.440 --> 01:02:17.108
You want help?
There's none coming.

01:02:17.109 --> 01:02:19.569
You're scared? You should be.

01:02:19.570 --> 01:02:21.821
You fucking should be!

01:03:36.480 --> 01:03:38.106
There's no way back up.

01:03:38.815 --> 01:03:40.901
The dumbwaiter button's broken.

01:03:42.277 --> 01:03:44.363
I can't use it to get back up.

01:03:46.740 --> 01:03:48.617
I can't find a way out.

01:03:51.203 --> 01:03:53.038
I'm stuck down here.

01:04:29.491 --> 01:04:30.701
Yes!

01:05:03.358 --> 01:05:04.401
Right...

01:05:59.790 --> 01:06:01.500
Oh! Ah...

01:06:03.585 --> 01:06:05.337
Oh, fuckin' Jesus.

01:06:21.436 --> 01:06:22.604
Ah...

01:09:08.478 --> 01:09:10.522
I think there's someone
down here!

01:09:12.941 --> 01:09:14.818
I keep hearing something.

01:09:21.616 --> 01:09:23.159
Is someone there?

01:09:25.579 --> 01:09:28.081
Oh God! Oh...

01:10:35.482 --> 01:10:37.943
Three, two...

01:10:48.203 --> 01:10:49.829
Come on! Come on...

01:10:51.581 --> 01:10:52.749
Come on...

01:10:58.254 --> 01:10:59.631
Hello?

01:12:55.997 --> 01:12:57.373
Aah...

01:15:35.573 --> 01:15:36.658
Uh...

01:15:37.450 --> 01:15:38.868
- Jesus...
- Ah, Mal.

01:15:39.369 --> 01:15:40.827
I need your help.

01:15:40.828 --> 01:15:43.581
Jesus, Jerry.
What happened to you?

01:15:43.873 --> 01:15:46.500
Oh, Fergal. It doesn't matter.

01:15:46.501 --> 01:15:47.751
I need to get up here.

01:15:47.752 --> 01:15:49.127
I need to get this open.

01:15:49.128 --> 01:15:50.837
- What for?
- The American.

01:15:50.838 --> 01:15:52.632
Ohm, he went up there.

01:15:53.258 --> 01:15:55.593
- Ugh!
- Stop! Stop, stop.

01:15:56.386 --> 01:15:57.595
He's gone.

01:15:58.179 --> 01:15:59.471
What?

01:15:59.472 --> 01:16:02.516
Mr Cob sent me out here
to look for the key,

01:16:02.517 --> 01:16:04.101
and when I got here,
the gate was unlocked,

01:16:04.102 --> 01:16:05.895
so I went up.
- And?

01:16:06.980 --> 01:16:09.190
- What did you find?
- Mr Bauman.

01:16:09.315 --> 01:16:11.943
- Drunk.
- What?

01:16:12.318 --> 01:16:15.320
- Where is he?
- He's on his way to the airport.

01:16:15.321 --> 01:16:17.948
Well, he was too drunk to drive,
so I took him down to town,

01:16:17.949 --> 01:16:19.909
stuffed him in a taxi
and sent him off.

01:16:20.118 --> 01:16:21.786
And Fiona?

01:16:23.079 --> 01:16:24.289
No.

01:17:28.519 --> 01:17:29.729
Hey...

01:17:33.816 --> 01:17:35.485
So, you just jumped?

01:17:36.527 --> 01:17:38.154
I mean, you could
have been killed.

01:17:44.285 --> 01:17:45.952
Are you sure
you checked that room?

01:17:45.953 --> 01:17:47.704
I mean, you looked everywhere?

01:17:47.705 --> 01:17:49.373
The room's not that big.

01:17:49.374 --> 01:17:52.502
She's not there.
I swear to you, I looked.

01:17:52.877 --> 01:17:54.712
I need to see it for myself.

01:17:56.172 --> 01:17:58.257
Fiona wants me to go up there.

01:17:58.383 --> 01:18:01.093
I'm going to have to call
the guards

01:18:01.094 --> 01:18:02.720
to tell them you're here.

01:18:06.599 --> 01:18:08.559
They know about your wife.

01:18:12.397 --> 01:18:13.648
I saw her...

01:18:14.690 --> 01:18:16.067
I saw her.

01:18:17.902 --> 01:18:19.821
Just go, Jerry.

01:18:20.363 --> 01:18:23.741
Take Bauman's car
and don't come back.

01:18:24.575 --> 01:18:26.619
I'll tell them
that you were already gone.

01:18:29.163 --> 01:18:30.581
Just go.

01:19:53.664 --> 01:19:55.248
No, no, no! Jerry!

01:19:55.249 --> 01:19:56.375
Jerry!

01:20:19.440 --> 01:20:20.441
Jerry!

01:20:20.816 --> 01:20:21.984
Jerry!

01:20:27.073 --> 01:20:28.199
Aah...

01:20:50.805 --> 01:20:52.139
Uh!

01:20:52.557 --> 01:20:53.683
Ah!

01:20:57.144 --> 01:20:58.521
I left the keys.

01:21:04.110 --> 01:21:05.736
Motherfucker...

01:21:09.407 --> 01:21:10.825
Are you all right, Mal?

01:21:11.242 --> 01:21:14.036
No, I'm-I'm actually
not feeling the best.

01:21:15.037 --> 01:21:18.332
I think I might need to lock up
and go home.

01:21:18.833 --> 01:21:20.918
Hey, why don't I get the keys
and I'll bring them out to you?

01:22:07.340 --> 01:22:09.425
God damn it!

01:22:38.829 --> 01:22:44.919
♪ Oft, in the stilly night ♪

01:22:45.252 --> 01:22:51.509
♪ Ere slumber's chain
has bound me ♪

01:22:53.427 --> 01:22:59.517
♪ Fond memory
brings the light ♪

01:23:00.935 --> 01:23:03.479
- Jerry.
- Fiona used to say,

01:23:04.522 --> 01:23:07.233
never ignore when something
feels off.

01:23:11.153 --> 01:23:13.239
Something feels off here, Mal.

01:23:13.406 --> 01:23:14.448
Jerry...

01:23:15.658 --> 01:23:16.741
You have to leave.

01:23:16.742 --> 01:23:18.410
If you dropped Ohm into town,

01:23:18.411 --> 01:23:20.204
why did you come back out here?

01:23:23.290 --> 01:23:26.252
To get this...
reframed for my wife.

01:23:28.379 --> 01:23:30.589
You drove all the way back out
here for that?

01:23:30.923 --> 01:23:32.674
Can't a man do something
nice for his wife

01:23:32.675 --> 01:23:33.925
without having
something to hide?

01:23:47.732 --> 01:23:49.483
- Uh...
- Jerry...

01:23:49.734 --> 01:23:51.276
Jerry, what the fuck
are you doing?

01:23:51.277 --> 01:23:53.111
- Key!
- I don't have it.

01:23:53.112 --> 01:23:54.529
I gave it back to Mr Cob.

01:23:54.530 --> 01:23:55.740
Give it to me!

01:23:56.323 --> 01:23:59.076
Okay. Okay, okay.

01:24:04.582 --> 01:24:06.292
Jerry, please.

01:24:06.542 --> 01:24:08.002
It was a mistake.

01:24:08.127 --> 01:24:09.711
You don't know Fiona like I did.

01:24:09.712 --> 01:24:11.171
She wasn't a good person!

01:24:11.172 --> 01:24:13.257
You know, she was threatening
to tell Mr Cob!

01:24:13.841 --> 01:24:15.633
And he hates me!

01:24:15.634 --> 01:24:18.429
He's threatened to have me
killed for less over the years!

01:24:19.180 --> 01:24:20.472
Just leave him!

01:24:20.473 --> 01:24:22.599
He was gonna
kill himself anyway!

01:24:31.942 --> 01:24:37.323
♪ I've seen
around me fall ♪

01:24:38.115 --> 01:24:44.663
♪ Like leaves
in wintry weather ♪

01:24:45.664 --> 01:24:48.667
♪ I feel like one ♪

01:24:49.251 --> 01:24:52.004
♪ Who treads alone ♪

01:24:52.588 --> 01:24:58.761
♪ Some banquet-hall deserted ♪

01:25:05.226 --> 01:25:08.103
- Ohm!
- Hey! Jerry!

01:25:08.562 --> 01:25:11.272
I'm in here! Get me
the fuck out of here, man!

01:25:18.948 --> 01:25:20.533
There's a small door here!

01:25:21.659 --> 01:25:23.244
I can bust it open.

01:25:23.994 --> 01:25:25.329
Yeah.

01:25:25.454 --> 01:25:26.831
Stay back, stay back.

01:25:28.666 --> 01:25:30.000
Uh!

01:25:35.089 --> 01:25:36.631
- Fiona?
- No, she's dead.

01:25:36.632 --> 01:25:38.259
Mal fucking killed her.

01:25:40.427 --> 01:25:41.554
Are you okay?

01:25:42.721 --> 01:25:44.264
I'll live.

01:25:44.265 --> 01:25:45.391
Uh!

01:26:03.117 --> 01:26:05.327
Don't try and leave!

01:26:05.703 --> 01:26:07.037
I mean it!

01:26:27.641 --> 01:26:29.935
Oh, fuck!

01:26:30.477 --> 01:26:31.854
Aaargh!

01:26:33.314 --> 01:26:35.274
God! Fuck!

01:27:12.394 --> 01:27:13.687
Bauman?

01:27:17.942 --> 01:27:19.193
Fuck...

01:27:22.529 --> 01:27:23.781
Bauman!

01:27:48.305 --> 01:27:49.974
Bauman, listen to me.

01:27:50.557 --> 01:27:52.266
The hotel is on fire.

01:27:52.267 --> 01:27:54.311
There's no way out down there.

01:27:54.645 --> 01:27:56.771
I'll bring you back up
with the key

01:27:56.772 --> 01:27:58.273
and we can both leave.

01:27:58.399 --> 01:28:00.025
You can go home.

01:28:01.026 --> 01:28:02.111
Bauman!

01:28:02.778 --> 01:28:04.196
Can you hear me?

01:28:20.838 --> 01:28:22.089
Ohm...

01:28:48.949 --> 01:28:50.284
Bauman?

01:30:09.404 --> 01:30:10.823
Ah!

01:30:12.449 --> 01:30:13.659
Uh!

01:31:06.879 --> 01:31:08.839
It was an accident.

01:31:12.384 --> 01:31:16.054
I'm sorry, it was an accident.

01:31:16.388 --> 01:31:17.681
I know.

01:31:21.101 --> 01:31:22.895
You can't stay here.

01:31:28.567 --> 01:31:30.569
It was an accident.

01:31:58.138 --> 01:31:59.473
What's happening?

01:32:20.827 --> 01:32:21.912
Help!

01:32:28.001 --> 01:32:29.253
Please! No!

01:32:38.595 --> 01:32:40.180
Aaaargh!

01:34:52.104 --> 01:34:53.313
Mal!

01:34:56.858 --> 01:34:57.984
Mal!

01:34:59.903 --> 01:35:00.904
Mal!

01:35:01.905 --> 01:35:03.323
Can you hear me?

01:35:05.367 --> 01:35:06.701
Ohm's Mum: Fergal!

01:35:08.787 --> 01:35:10.414
Is there someone there?

01:35:16.711 --> 01:35:18.130
Jesus...

01:35:18.922 --> 01:35:20.507
Hey! Hey, hey, hey!

01:35:21.007 --> 01:35:22.884
Come on, we have to go! Up!

01:35:27.222 --> 01:35:28.932
Come on! We have to go!

01:35:48.368 --> 01:35:50.370
How are you feeling, Mr Bauman?

01:35:55.333 --> 01:35:56.585
You're that bellboy.

01:35:57.502 --> 01:35:58.795
My name's Alby.

01:35:59.629 --> 01:36:01.172
I didn't think you'd have
anybody visiting you,

01:36:01.173 --> 01:36:02.424
being away from home.

01:36:02.757 --> 01:36:05.302
I'm not sure I'd have anybody
visiting me there either.

01:36:08.096 --> 01:36:09.555
Sit down, sorry.

01:36:14.519 --> 01:36:17.731
Okay. Uh, I guess I'll just get
two scoops of vanilla.

01:36:18.190 --> 01:36:22.109
Yeah, I work in the ice cream
parlour next door as well, yeah.

01:36:22.110 --> 01:36:23.236
Ah.

01:36:23.653 --> 01:36:25.530
Oh, this is from Fergal.

01:36:27.949 --> 01:36:30.118
He's pretty devastated
about Fiona.

01:36:30.368 --> 01:36:32.161
He said if you needed anything
to let him know.

01:36:32.162 --> 01:36:33.747
Yeah, I spoke to him
on the phone.

01:36:33.997 --> 01:36:34.956
Oh.

01:36:36.208 --> 01:36:37.792
You been to the hotel?

01:36:38.001 --> 01:36:39.377
What's left of it.

01:36:40.837 --> 01:36:42.339
They found remains.

01:36:42.923 --> 01:36:44.549
Fiona and Jerry.

01:36:47.761 --> 01:36:48.970
Mal?

01:36:49.137 --> 01:36:50.931
His car was found outside.

01:36:51.181 --> 01:36:52.724
They're looking for him.

01:36:57.437 --> 01:37:00.857
Mr Bauman, I need
to tell you something.

01:37:03.652 --> 01:37:06.154
I don't what happened, um,

01:37:06.530 --> 01:37:09.449
but I'm worried it might have
been my fault in some way.

01:37:10.617 --> 01:37:11.743
How?

01:37:12.869 --> 01:37:15.205
There was a flask of whiskey
in your room.

01:37:16.331 --> 01:37:18.667
- Did you drink it?
- Yeah.

01:37:19.167 --> 01:37:20.460
Much of it?

01:37:20.835 --> 01:37:23.588
Well, it's whiskey.
I drink all of it. Why?

01:37:25.215 --> 01:37:26.716
I spiked it.

01:37:28.134 --> 01:37:29.636
With what?

01:37:30.345 --> 01:37:32.722
I had some of Jerry's
mushroom powder.

01:37:33.014 --> 01:37:36.059
I snuck into your room
and I put it in the flask.

01:37:38.144 --> 01:37:39.688
Why would you do that?

01:37:40.021 --> 01:37:41.564
Well, it was after
I tried to speak to you

01:37:41.565 --> 01:37:42.899
at the bar that night.

01:37:44.067 --> 01:37:45.734
You burnt my hand.

01:37:45.735 --> 01:37:47.112
That hurt.

01:37:50.490 --> 01:37:53.201
You know, all these
things do exist.

01:37:53.577 --> 01:37:57.289
It's just people with closed
minds can't see 'em.

01:38:01.751 --> 01:38:03.086
I'm sorry.

01:38:04.004 --> 01:38:05.839
You were really rude.

01:38:08.383 --> 01:38:10.427
I'd better go
before they kick me out.

01:38:10.927 --> 01:38:13.847
One of the firemen
found this at the hotel.

01:38:22.897 --> 01:38:24.524
Hey, um...

01:38:25.942 --> 01:38:27.444
you can take that, too.

01:38:28.236 --> 01:38:29.570
I didn't touch it.

01:38:29.571 --> 01:38:31.239
Yeah, no, just, just take it.

01:38:35.744 --> 01:38:37.786
If you wanted something
to pass the time,

01:38:37.787 --> 01:38:38.913
I could bring in my manuscript.

01:38:41.291 --> 01:38:43.543
I mean, I've been
through enough already, Alby.

01:38:46.421 --> 01:38:48.465
I'll do a quick polish tonight
and drop it in tomorrow.

01:38:49.507 --> 01:38:50.550
All right.

01:39:34.886 --> 01:39:36.805
I said turn away!

01:39:54.614 --> 01:39:55.907
Aaargh!

01:40:07.293 --> 01:40:08.420
Here.

01:40:09.546 --> 01:40:10.964
Hit me here.

01:40:12.590 --> 01:40:15.552
As hard as you can.
You understand?

01:40:17.345 --> 01:40:18.930
You don't stop for blood.

01:40:19.055 --> 01:40:20.264
You don't stop for bone

01:40:20.265 --> 01:40:22.976
and you keep hitting
until it breaks.

01:40:25.145 --> 01:40:27.689
Follows the map and you claim it
all as yours.

01:40:31.401 --> 01:40:33.361
It's nothing I don't deserve.

01:40:39.784 --> 01:40:41.578
Do it before I change my mind.

01:40:43.079 --> 01:40:44.038
No.

01:40:44.164 --> 01:40:45.248
No...

01:42:16.673 --> 01:42:21.260
♪ Farewell vain world
I'm going home ♪

01:42:21.261 --> 01:42:25.056
♪ My saviour smiles
and bids me come ♪

01:42:25.223 --> 01:42:28.518
♪ And I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:42:28.726 --> 01:42:33.064
♪ Sweet angels
beckon me away ♪

01:42:33.189 --> 01:42:36.901
♪ To sing God's praise
in endless day ♪

01:42:37.110 --> 01:42:40.405
♪ And I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:42:40.530 --> 01:42:43.490
♪ Right up yonder ♪

01:42:43.491 --> 01:42:47.036
♪ Christians away up yonder ♪

01:42:47.287 --> 01:42:49.746
♪ Oh yes, my Lord ♪

01:42:49.747 --> 01:42:53.459
♪ For I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:42:54.043 --> 01:42:58.381
♪ I'm glad that I am
born to die ♪

01:42:58.506 --> 01:43:02.260
♪ From grief and woe
my soul shall fly ♪

01:43:02.427 --> 01:43:05.638
♪ And I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:43:05.847 --> 01:43:10.059
♪ Bright angels
shall convey me home ♪

01:43:10.226 --> 01:43:13.897
♪ Away to New Jerusalem ♪

01:43:14.105 --> 01:43:17.275
♪ And I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:43:17.483 --> 01:43:20.361
♪ Right up yonder ♪

01:43:20.486 --> 01:43:23.823
♪ Christians away up yonder ♪

01:43:24.157 --> 01:43:26.617
♪ Oh yes, my Lord ♪

01:43:26.618 --> 01:43:29.787
♪ For I don't care
to stay here long ♪

01:43:29.996 --> 01:43:32.874
♪ Right up yonder ♪

01:43:32.999 --> 01:43:36.461
♪ Christians away up yonder ♪

01:43:36.586 --> 01:43:39.005
♪ Oh yes, my Lord ♪

01:43:39.130 --> 01:43:43.384
♪ For I don't care
